
This directory contains project tests.

Level progress host regression (from the repository root):

```sh
cc -std=c11 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -I ESP32/include \
  ESP32/test/test_level_progress.c ESP32/src/esp_player_fresh_map_state.c \
  ESP32/src/esp_map_catalog.c -o /tmp/test_level_progress
/tmp/test_level_progress
```

The production progress owner and map catalog are compiled unchanged; only the
player/HUD view boundaries are mocked. Tests cover fresh map entry, XP baseline
across a level-up, elapsed-time resume without offline/loading time, legacy-save
partial history, rejected malformed suffixes, timer wrap and counter saturation.

SYS direct-touch host regression (from the repository root):

```sh
cc -std=c11 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -I ESP32/include \
  ESP32/test/test_sys_touch.c ESP32/src/esp_native_gameplay_save_touch.c \
  -o /tmp/test_sys_touch
/tmp/test_sys_touch
```

The production touch wrapper is compiled unchanged; its HUB cursor/navigation
and input boundaries are mocked. Checks cover every content pixel against the
shared three-card layout, rejection of gaps/margins, all nine cursor-to-target
routes, failed/invalid preselection, empty input and non-SYS fallback. These
tests do not replace hardware confirmation of SAVE/LOAD or Exit To Menu.

Death-menu presentation / input host regression (from the repository root):

```sh
cc -std=c11 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -ffunction-sections -fdata-sections \
  -I ESP32/include -I src ESP32/test/test_death_menu.c \
  ESP32/src/esp_native_gameplay_player_death.c \
  ESP32/src/esp_native_gameplay_hub_touch_ui.c \
  -Wl,--gc-sections -o /tmp/test_death_menu
/tmp/test_death_menu
# Optional: export the real painter at physical 320x240 for visual inspection.
/tmp/test_death_menu /tmp/death-with-save.ppm /tmp/death-no-save.ppm
```

Production death/menu code and the shared HUB font are compiled unchanged.
Clock, player/view/HUD, framebuffer/present and checkpoint boundaries are mocked.
Checks cover the fall and three-second menu admission, shared palette/text,
with/without save, card corners/gaps/margins, queued LOAD, unchanged deferred
routes, framebuffer guards and failed presentation. This does not validate
actual SD restore, combat or display behavior on the CYD.

Unit Testing is a software testing method by which individual units of
source code, sets of one or more MCU program modules together with associated
control data, usage procedures, and operating procedures, are tested to
determine whether they are fit for use. Unit testing finds problems early
in the development cycle.

More information about PlatformIO Unit Testing:
- https://docs.platformio.org/en/latest/advanced/unit-testing/index.html
